SUMMARY:[Federal Maine-Related] Hours of Service of Drivers: Association o
 f American Railroads and American Short Line and Regional Railroad Associa
 tion\; Application for Exemption Renewal
DESCRIPTION:FMCSA announces its final decision to renew and modify the exe
 mption granted to the Association of American Railroads and the American S
 hort Line and Regional Railroad Association and member railroads (the Asso
 ciations) from the hours-of-service (HOS) prohibitions against driving aft
 er the 14th hour after coming on duty (the 14-hour rule) and against drivi
 ng after accumulating 60 hours of on duty time within 7 consecutive days\,
  or 70 hours of on duty time within 8 consecutive days (the 60-hour/70-hou
 r rule). The exemption will enable covered drivers to respond to unplanned
  events that occur outside of\, or extend beyond\, their normal work hours
 . FMCSA modifies the previous exemption to limit the categories of unplann
 ed events during which the exemption may be used and to add reporting requ
 irements. In addition\, only drivers operating for motor carriers listed i
 n the Appendix to this decision may operate under the exemption. FMCSA has
  analyzed the exemption application and has determined that the exemption 
 renewal\, subject to the terms and conditions set forth below\, is likely 
 to achieve a level of safety that is equivalent to or greater than the lev
 el that would be achieved in the absence of the exemption.\nhttps://www.fe
 deralregister.gov/documents/2026/10/21/2026-21488/hours-of-service-of-driv
 ers-association-of-american-railroads-and-american-short-line-and-regional
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/21/2026-21488/hours-
 of-service-of-drivers-association-of-american-railroads-and-american-short
 -line-and-regional
CATEGORIES:Federal Maine-Related
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
